  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x1358">
    <title>F132 Table Value Selector (X=MAT, 0=InletTemp)</title>
    <description>inlet temp is a calculated value based on air temp, airflow, coolant temp and time, used to simulate the fact that as the intake manifold and heads warm up, the air inside them warms as well, which causes it to change density and has a different fueling requirement.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;most, if not all, A1 BINs use inlettemp instead of MAT, so the table is labeled as such.</description>
